  "summary": "I added a \"Lights off\" button below the canvas and the `window.__TASK_STATE__` readout. Typecheck passes, and I checked both lighting states with a screenshot render. I haven't clicked the button in a browser, so the click-to-toggle behavior itself is untested.\n\n- **Toggle:** clicking the button rebuilds the scene with `app.setScene`. Lights off uses the dim blue `polar-night` look at exposure -1.2, with the two warm lamps near the clock kept on at lower intensity so the face and pendulum stay readable. Lights on restores the original `interior-warm` look and lamp settings. The button label switches between \"Lights off\" and \"Lights on\".\n- **Night check:** I rendered the night state once by temporarily starting the page with lights off. The face and hands were readable against a dim room. I then reverted the default to lights on.\n- **State object:** `window.__TASK_STATE__ = { lightsOn, pendulumAngleDeg }` is updated every frame. The angle is signed degrees from vertical, and positive means the bob is to the right on screen.\n- **Files:** the button is in `index.html`; the toggle logic and state object are in `src/main.ts`."
